## Step 3 — Decide the fix set (no approval gate)
Choose from this menu:
1. Title/meta rewrite.
2. Freshness refresh: a new section and/or a replaced stale section, current-season trend lines, re-labeled dated copy.
3. Content-gap section (B bucket), with a 40–60 word direct-answer capsule opening it.
4. Terminology/definitions paragraph.
5. Trim (C2).
6. Internal links (only when the Live URLs file is present).
7. Stale or wrong FAQ/tldr answers.
8. American spelling pass.
9. Expert quote (only if alias + answer were supplied).

**Size rule:** a freshness update changes roughly 20–30% of the page's text with real content. Never a bare date bump. If the content is healthy and not stale and the fix is title/meta only, change only the title/meta and **leave `dateModified` alone**.

**Defaults, applied without asking:**
- Images: reuse existing ones only; never generate. A new section uses no new image. Never add a new numbered entry/design that would need its own image.
- No expert quote unless alias + full answer were supplied.
- No new internal links unless the Live URLs file is present.

