## Editing mechanics (follow exactly)
1. **Work from the real file.** Fetch the raw URL into the container (raw.githubusercontent.com is allowed) or use the uploaded/pasted file. Never retype the file.
2. **Edit with a script** using exact-match replacements that assert exactly one match. Untouched text stays byte-identical. Never regenerate the page.
3. **Frontmatter you may edit:** `title`, `excerpt`, `dateModified` (only if the body changed materially), `wordCount`, `tldr`/`faqItems` text where stale or wrong, `expert` (if a quote is placed).
   **Never touch:** `slug`, `canonical`, `date`, `author`, `category`, `topic`, image fields, `tags`, `topicalMap`, `navigationContext`, `sameAs`, `template`. If one looks wrong, flag it.
4. **Body structure:** the H2 structure stays as is, with two exceptions: a planned freshness section may be added, and a thin/stale seasonal section may be replaced. Mention both in the summary. Existing internal and external links stay verbatim (href and anchor text); carry them into any section you replace. `<img>` blocks stay byte-identical (src, alt, dimensions).
5. **Spelling:** American English throughout the body and frontmatter text fields (`title`, `excerpt`, `tldr`, `faqItems`, `imageCaption`). Do not alter `<img>` blocks, filenames, `imageAlt`, `tags`, or the slug; list what remains.
6. **`wordCount`:** keep the file's own counting method by adding the word delta (tags stripped, split on whitespace) to the existing value.
7. **Verify before delivering:** diff shows only intended changes; zero long em dashes; no banned words in new text; leftover British spellings listed; count of double-space artifacts (left by stripped dashes) reported, not fixed unless asked.
8. **Save** to `/mnt/user-data/outputs/<slug>.md` and present it.

