## Standing lessons from this site (check on every page)
- Many pages sit at position 1–3 with CTR under 0.1% on head terms. Treat as a SERP-feature signature first, title problem second.
- Titles with a false number ("30+ ideas") or a promise the body doesn't keep are common; check before writing anything.
- Seasonal copy goes stale fast: re-angle to the current season using today's date.
- Cross-check internal consistency when touching FAQ/tldr (group numbers, design numbers, counts).
- Dash removal elsewhere left double spaces in several files; report the count.
- Frontmatter FAQ/tldr often still carry British spellings after a body pass; sweep them.
- Judge CTR against the site's own baseline in the same export, not only the 1.5% rule. When site-wide CTR is ~0.2%, a page at 1%+ is a winner: protect its title.
- Position-1 impressions across many sibling pages for one contains-match query is a SERP-feature pattern, not cannibalization.
